{
 "$comment": "raea effects catalog (docs/ENGINE-COMPLETENESS.md, effects). Source of truth for the apps' Settings > Effects list and the Agent's effect vocabulary. status: stable (on by default) | beta (off by default, listed under Beta effects). needs: ML tracks an effect reads (segmentation, depth, landmarks), produced on device. dsl: the one-line form a composition uses (data-fx). Entries are added as each effect renders like Chrome and passes the Agent eval. params: each argument in order: name, type (length = px number, color = any CSS colour, hexcolor = #rgb/#rrggbb/rgb(), number, time = seconds like 0.2s or 200ms, times = a space-separated list of times, enum), default, min/max or values. Any length or number argument can be a range \"a..b\" (e.g. blur(0px..12px)): it animates from a to b over the element's time on screen; \"a..b..c@0s..1s..2s\" sets keyframes at those times.",
 "version": 1,
